arguments.content:
💡 **SUGGESTION: record the deliberate lint suppression in the code, not just the PR body**

The `prefer_initializing_formals` info here is unavoidable (the analyzer suggests `this._home`, but a private named formal would remove the `home:` named argument the tests and any caller rely on), and CI runs `flutter analyze --no-fatal-infos` so it passes. Still, a reader of this file sees an analyzer warning with no explanation — the rationale lives only in the PR description. A one-line ignore keeps the intent in the code:

```dart
}) : environment = environment ?? Platform.environment,
     // ignore: prefer_initializing_formals — `this._home` would have to be a
     // private NAMED formal (drops the public `home:` arg); `home` backs the
     // resolveDapHome getter below.
     _home = home;
```

